                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sedenion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "02a01b1e-67ee-3e89-90c3-626189c08ed0",
                                        "entry_id": "214d0961-7d30-358a-821e-069b6b8124c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A 16-dimensional nonalternative extension of an octonion with one real part and 15 imaginary parts, each a real multiple of a distinct, independent square root of −1."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c398ca8-f1ea-42a5-b33c-1bb31d7b1e09",
                                                "sense_id": "02a01b1e-67ee-3e89-90c3-626189c08ed0",
                                                "text": "According to the logic of doubling the dimensions on which Cayley–Dickson algebra is built, after quaternions the so-called 8D octonions (#92;mathbbO—Octonions) can be obtained, followed by 16D sedenions, 32D pathions, 64D chingons, 128D routons, and 256D voudons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e4da373-2cd3-4479-a264-6cb3255dcfc2",
                                                "sense_id": "02a01b1e-67ee-3e89-90c3-626189c08ed0",
                                                "text": "There is no theoretical limit to multispace dimensional numbering as there are definitions for octonion (8D), sedenion (16D), pathion (32D), chingon (64D), routon (128D), and voudon (256D) numbered space."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
